        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both ICs are assembled, they can drive shared GPIO nets to opposing levels, causing excessive current, unreliable fan control, or damage. If one is an intended alternative, the assembly files need to ensure only one is fitted.",
